    "nodeGroups": [],
    "authors": "Ramon ramon@pereirariosoftware.com (via MCP)",
    "name": "Split BTC onto its own 2-hourly schedule; remove unused wallet-balance branch",
    "description": "Removed the temp delete node and the now-unused wallet-balance branch (Set Wallet Balance, BTC Wallet Address, Get Wallet Balance, Compute BTC Balance, Update Firefly Balance) since the account it targeted no longer exists. Split scheduling: fiat rates (EUR->BRL,GBP) stay on the 18:00 Lisbon trigger (after ECB publishes); BTC/EUR now runs on its own new trigger every 2 hours, independent of the fiat branch. Note: Firefly only stores one rate per calendar day per pair, so intraday BTC runs overwrite the same day's row rather than building intraday history -- confirmed via two same-day posts landing on the same row IDs with updated_at bumped.",
    "autosaved": false
